# CODEOWNERS
#
# This file designates individuals or teams responsible for reviewing code changes.
# When a pull request modifies a file matching a pattern below, GitHub automatically
# requests a review from the designated owner(s).
#
# Rules are matched in order — the last matching rule takes precedence.
# Owners must have write access to the repository.
#
# Syntax:
#   <pattern>   @<username-or-team>
#
# Documentation:
#   https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default owner — fallback for all files not matched by a more specific rule
*       @<username>

# Examples — uncomment and customize as needed:
# src/auth/*          @<username>          # Auth module
# src/api/*           @<username>          # API layer
# docs/*              @<username>          # Documentation
# .github/*           @<username>          # CI/CD and repo config
# *.md                @<username>          # All Markdown files
